; AlifePlus outpost stock policy. Filters a conquered-area service NPC's player-facing stock
; after each restock, so a field outpost sells a lean assortment instead of the full faction
; shelf. Applied on top of the below-hub supplies drop (Mutators > Conquest); this file decides
; WHICH kinds a service stocks, the supplies drop decides HOW DEEP its ammo/gear tiers go.
;
; FORMAT (same shape as ap_loot_policy.ltx): `category = min, max`. MAX is used, MIN is ignored.
;   max = 0  -> the category is stripped from stock (blacklist).
;   max = N  -> the category is kept, capped at N (whitelist with a cap).
;   a row deleted entirely -> that category is left untouched.
;   a row may also name a single item section (energy_drink = 0, 2); a section row overrides
;   the item's category row, same contract as the other policy files.
; DLTX-overridable like the other policy files. Absent or empty file = filter off (logged).
;
; MEANING -- differs from the loadout policies (ap_trade_policy, ap_loot_policy) by design, and
; this is the whole reason it is a separate file. Those cap a category TOTAL across what one NPC
; CARRIES. This caps PER TYPE on what a trader SELLS: a shelf stocks many kinds, a loadout is one
; carry. So `medkit = 0, 3` keeps 3 of EACH medkit kind on the shelf, and `ammo_per_type = 0, 90`
; keeps 90 rounds of EACH ammo type (two ammo types of one caliber keep 90 each; the key is the
; shelf equivalent of the loadout policies' equipped-relative ammo_slot_* keys, in rounds).
; Whole stacks release: an ammo cap below one box size strips that type entirely rather than
; keeping a partial box.
;
; Category names match get_section_category (the same vocabulary the other policies use).
; Equipped weapon and armor and quest items are never in scope -- the categorizer skips them.
;
; DEFAULT below = a field resupply post: ammo, medical, provisions, a few grenades and repair
; parts; no weapons, armor, artefacts, or devices (an outpost is not an armory).

[ap_outpost_stock]
ammo_per_type    = 0, 90
grenade_ammo     = 0, 2
medkit           = 0, 3
bandage          = 0, 5
antirad          = 0, 3
stim             = 0, 2
pill             = 0, 2
food             = 0, 5
drink            = 0, 5
grenade          = 0, 2
crafting         = 0, 5
weapon           = 0, 0
outfit           = 0, 0
helmet           = 0, 0
artefact         = 0, 0
device           = 0, 0
other            = 0, 0
